{"version":3,"kind":"Article","sha256":"a070a7fb333279e583164b2fc33cbe91d39f42624af2b4a6e25b2ff8e36c4590","slug":"ch03.cdfs","location":"/ch03/03-03-cdfs.md","dependencies":[],"frontmatter":{"title":"3.3 Standard notations and common functions","content_includes_title":false,"github":"https://github.com/jpowerj/clrs","numbering":{"title":{"offset":1}},"source_url":"https://github.com/jpowerj/clrs/blob/main/ch03/03-03-cdfs.md","edit_url":"https://github.com/jpowerj/clrs/edit/main/ch03/03-03-cdfs.md","exports":[{"format":"md","filename":"03-03-cdfs.md","url":"/03-03-cdfs-1b8aa17b4c199e1464c2ec01422b767d.md"}]},"mdast":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"This section reviews some standard mathematical functions and notations and explores the relationships among them. It also illustrates the use of the asymptotic notations.","position":{"start":{"line":4,"column":1},"end":{"line":4,"column":1}},"key":"Bmf90Ikluy"}],"key":"Of2cj6OBQm"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Monotonicity","position":{"start":{"line":6,"column":1},"end":{"line":6,"column":1}},"key":"uJwd1kCj5Q"}],"key":"rV8LeW73ye"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":11,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function f .n/ is monotonically increasing if m හ n implies f .m/ හ f .n/.\nSimilarly, it is monotonically decreasing if m හ n implies f .m/  f .n/. A func-\ntion f .n/ is strictly increasing if m < n implies f .m/ < f .n/ and strictly de-\ncreasing if m < n implies f .m/ > f .n/","position":{"start":{"line":8,"column":1},"end":{"line":8,"column":1}},"key":"IDmBtO22oK"}],"key":"eVBqczWbLA"}],"key":"KKW3Tg90Yd"}],"key":"OQWK3VWvem"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}}}